---
import Chapter from "../components/Chapter.astro";
import { consent, seed, stats } from "../data/facts";
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, "");
const guide = (slug: string) => `${base}/guide/${slug}`;

const clauses = [
  { lead: "Patients", rest: "own their history." },
  { lead: "Providers", rest: "contribute to it." },
  { lead: "Clinicians", rest: "read it only with the patient's consent." },
  { lead: "Every access", rest: "is recorded." },
];
---

<Chapter
  id="promise"
  n={2}
  title="Four rules, each enforced by something that cannot be skipped"
  lede="Pulse is one sentence in four clauses. None of them is a policy document. Each is held in place by a table shape, a query, a test or a database grant."
  wide
>
  <div class="prm" data-steps>
    <div class="prm__inv">
      <ol class="inv" aria-label="The invariant, built one clause at a time">
        {clauses.map((c) => (
          <li><strong>{c.lead}</strong> {c.rest}</li>
        ))}
      </ol>
    </div>

    <div class="prm__steps">
      <article class="step" data-step>
        <h3>Patients own their history</h3>
        <p>
          The Patient row is the root of everything clinical. Medical Entries, data-quality flags and duplicate-review
          items all point at <code>patient.id</code>. There is no separate "patient record" entity that could drift from
          the person.
        </p>
        <p>
          <code>patient.user_id</code> is nullable on purpose. A Patient can exist before the person has an account, so a
          Provider can file for someone who has never registered. The demo data has {seed.unclaimed} of its {seed.patients}
          patients in that state. The screen that creates an unclaimed Patient, and the step where the person later claims
          it, are not built; filing for an existing Patient ID is.
        </p>
        <p class="how">
          <a href={guide("adr/0002-patient-is-the-aggregate-root")}>ADR-0002</a>
          <a href={guide("domain-model")}>Domain model</a>
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="step" data-step>
        <h3>Providers contribute to it</h3>
        <p>
          Provider Staff are the only role that holds <code>RECORDS_WRITE</code>. They file any of the {stats.entryKinds} kinds
          of Medical Entry and attach documents. Nobody edits or deletes an entry afterwards: a correction inserts a
          new one and stamps the original as superseded, so the history shows what was believed and when.
        </p>
        <p>
          Contributing is not reading. Staff list back only the entries their own provider authored, and the Patient can
          read all of them.
        </p>
        <p class="how">
          <a href="#people">Who holds which permission</a>
          <a href={guide("adr/0001-medical-entry-joined-table-inheritance")}>ADR-0001</a>
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="step" data-step>
        <h3>Clinicians read it only with the patient's consent</h3>
        <p>
          A role alone opens nothing. A Clinician reads a Patient's entries through a consent that names that Clinician,
          limits the entry types and an optional date window, and expires within {consent.minDays} to {consent.maxDays} days. Consent goes to a person, never to a hospital, so agreeing to it can mean something.
        </p>
        <p>
          The check is part of the SQL, in one query builder every read goes through. A refused read returns 404, so a
          refusal does not reveal that the person is a patient at all.
        </p>
        <p>
          There is one deliberate exception. A Clinician can request {consent.breakGlassMinutes}-minute emergency access
          with a written reason, and the Patient is shown a banner on their timeline.
        </p>
        <p class="how">
          <a href="#consent-engine">The consent engine, try it</a>
          <a href={guide("adr/0006-consent-enforced-by-one-query-builder")}>ADR-0006</a>
          <a href={guide("adr/0010-consent-is-granted-to-individuals")}>ADR-0010</a>
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="step" data-step>
        <h3>Every access is recorded</h3>
        <p>
          The service layer writes an Audit Event explicitly, once per access: a 50-entry timeline is one <code>ENTRY_VIEWED</code>, and a refused read writes <code>ACCESS_DENIED</code>. No clinical value ever goes
          into an event, so the log cannot become a second copy of the record.
        </p>
        <p>
          The application's database role holds only <code>INSERT</code> and <code>SELECT</code> on <code>audit_event</code>. The database refuses <code>UPDATE</code> and <code>DELETE</code>, even from our own
          code. The Patient reads their own log. An administrator audit viewer is not built.
        </p>
        <p class="how">
          <a href={guide("adr/0008-audit-log-is-append-only-by-grant")}>ADR-0008</a>
          <a href={guide("architecture")}>Architecture</a>
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="refuse">
    <h3 class="refuse__title">What Pulse refuses to do</h3>
    <dl>
      <div>
        <dt>No administrator reads clinical data</dt>
        <dd>
          The Administrator role holds no <code>RECORDS_READ</code>, and there is no override. Merging duplicate patients
          is decided from name, birth date, phone, address and entry counts, never from the entries.
          <a href={guide("adr/0007-administrators-cannot-read-clinical-data")}>ADR-0007</a>
        </dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt>No consent to an organisation</dt>
        <dd>
          Consent is granted to one named Clinician. Agreeing that a hospital may read a history means agreeing to an
          unbounded, changing set of people. A Clinician who changes jobs keeps their consents.
          <a href={guide("adr/0010-consent-is-granted-to-individuals")}>ADR-0010</a>
        </dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt>No real patient data, ever</dt>
        <dd>
          Every record is synthetic: Synthea {seed.synthea} output plus an Indian identity overlay, with generated names
          and phone numbers in a sentinel range. This is an academic project and never touches a real person.
          <a href={guide("adr/0015-synthea-plus-indian-overlay-seed-data")}>ADR-0015</a>
        </dd>
      </div>
    </dl>
  </div>
</Chapter>

<style>
  .prm { display: grid; gap: 1.5rem; }
  .prm__inv { align-self: start; }
  .inv { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; display: grid; gap: 0.4rem; }
  .inv li {
    padding-left: 0.9rem;
    border-left: 3px solid transparent;
    font-size: 1.12rem;
    line-height: 1.3;
    font-weight: 500;
    transition: opacity 400ms var(--ease-out), border-color 400ms var(--ease-out);
  }
  .inv strong { font-weight: 700; color: var(--primary); }

  /* The sentence builds clause by clause; the clause being explained carries a bar. */
  [data-active="0"] .inv li:nth-child(n + 2),
  [data-active="1"] .inv li:nth-child(n + 3),
  [data-active="2"] .inv li:nth-child(n + 4) { opacity: 0.2; }
  [data-active="0"] .inv li:nth-child(1),
  [data-active="1"] .inv li:nth-child(2),
  [data-active="2"] .inv li:nth-child(3),
  [data-active="3"] .inv li:nth-child(4) { border-left-color: var(--primary); }

  /* Narrow: the building sentence stays pinned under the header while the steps scroll. */
  .prm__inv {
    position: sticky;
    top: 63px;
    z-index: 5;
    margin-inline: calc(var(--content-start) * -1) calc(var(--gutter) * -1);
    padding: 0.75rem var(--gutter) 0.75rem var(--content-start);
    background: var(--glass-fill);
    backdrop-filter: blur(16px);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
  }
  .step { padding: 1.5rem 0 2rem; max-width: 56ch; }
  .step h3 { font-size: var(--step-2); margin-bottom: 0.9rem; }
  .step p + p { margin-top: 0.9em; }
  .step p { color: var(--muted-foreground); }
  .how { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.4rem 1.25rem; font-size: 0.95rem; }

  @media (min-width: 900px) {
    .prm { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 0.9fr) minmax(0, 1fr); gap: 4rem; }
    .prm__inv {
      top: 120px;
      margin: 0;
      padding: 0;
      background: none;
      backdrop-filter: none;
      border: 0;
    }
    .inv { gap: 1.1rem; }
    .inv li { font-size: var(--step-2); line-height: 1.15; padding-left: 1.25rem; letter-spacing: -0.015em; }
    .step { min-height: 62vh; padding: 3rem 0; }
  }

  .refuse { margin-top: clamp(4rem, 8vw, 7rem); padding-top: 2.5rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--border); max-width: 880px; }
  .refuse__title { font-size: var(--step-2); }
  .refuse dl { margin: 2rem 0 0; }
  .refuse dl > div { display: grid; gap: 0.4rem; padding: 1.25rem 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--border); }
  .refuse dl > div:last-child { border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); }
  .refuse dt { font-weight: 700; font-size: var(--step-1); line-height: 1.2; }
  .refuse dd { margin: 0; color: var(--muted-foreground); }
  .refuse dd a { white-space: nowrap; margin-left: 0.25rem; }
  @media (min-width: 800px) {
    .refuse dl > div { grid-template-columns: 15rem minmax(0, 1fr); gap: 2rem; }
  }
</style>
